Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:24:49 +0800
Subject: [11/14] docs: the slow drift is real and large (+73% over 160 ps)

Mid-run analysis of the 1.6 ns jobs (run_v042/v043) with the plane estimator in
20 ps windows: TBR_eff grows monotonically 1.06e-8 -> 1.83e-8 for flat and
1.12e-8 -> 1.82e-8 for P350, i.e. +73 % over 160 ps, with no sign of a plateau.

Consequences:
  * time_converged <= 5 % cannot be met at the 200 ps scale -- the measured
    quantity itself is changing, not just the noise;
  * every TBR reported so far is a snapshot, which explains the 3x spread
    between protocol generations in the re-ranking table;
  * the only stable statement is the relative one: P350 stays 5-7 % above flat
    at every time, i.e. grooves do not help.
